  <prompt>
    Validate the shipped session-dispatch path end-to-end for a single Compose capability BEFORE any Phase-1/3/4 work builds on it. Author a throwaway `compose-explain-clause` Action + Binding pair (mirror-first), wire a stub Workspace toolbar button that emits a PaneEventBus `compose_action_request` event, and confirm the full chain: PaneEventBus → ConversationPane → `dispatchConsumer(bindingId, args)` → `POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{id}/dispatch` → `SessionDispatchOrchestrator` → Binding resolution → prompted executor → SSE stream into the chat surface + a ledger `SessionOutput` write. This is a validation of the shipped path (the server surface is already answered), proving the Compose-specific legs: event payload shape, scope-payload assembly, and selection args. All artifacts are throwaway — the deliverable is a spike note recording whether the seam works and what the Compose-specific event/args contract must be.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior full-stack engineer fluent in .NET 8 Minimal API, the Spaarke session-dispatch seam (ADR-039), the ADR-040 session ledger, PaneEventBus choreography (ADR-030), and SSE streaming (ADR-033).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A spike note at projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/spikes/spike-0-dispatch-path.md that answers a single decision: is the shipped session-dispatch seam confirmed end-to-end for a Compose Binding? It must record, with evidence, (1) the PaneEventBus event shape a Compose toolbar click must emit, (2) the selection-args + scope-payload assembly the ConversationPane must perform, (3) proof of SSE streaming into the chat surface, (4) proof of a ledger `SessionOutput` write, and (5) confirmation the gate does not interfere for a Tier-0/1 action. No production code is committed.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §13 Spike 0 + §2.1 + §7.2: R2 introduces NO new AI dispatch endpoint (PR #544 killed the parallel Compose endpoint; ADR-039 makes the Binding table the only routing config). Every AI action flows through the shipped Click-path seam. Before authoring 5 real catalog rows (Phase 4) and the inline toolbar (Phase 3), this spike de-risks the Compose-specific legs of that seam with one throwaway Binding. Decision unlocked (design §13): confirms the end-to-end seam before Phase 1 builds on it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="dispatch-seam-client">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/dispatchConsumer.ts — dispatchConsumer(bindingId, args) → POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{id}/dispatch</file>
      <file purpose="dispatch-endpoint">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs — existing Compose endpoint group (reference only; do NOT add a dispatch route)</file>
      <file purpose="conversation-pane">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx — consumes compose_action_request, assembles args, calls dispatchConsumer</file>
      <file purpose="pre-seed-bridge">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler.cs — chat→Compose bridge reference for payload conventions</file>
      <file purpose="catalog-mirror">infra/dataverse/inputschemas/ — mirror-first location for the throwaway Action + Binding rows</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">No task dependencies — startable immediately (Wave W0).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Dispatch MUST go through the shipped session-dispatch seam only. Do NOT add a new BFF dispatch route. Routing config lives ONLY in the Binding table; string-key resolution outside it is banned. The throwaway Action + Binding pair is mirror-first under infra/dataverse/inputschemas/.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">The dispatched response MUST be written to the session ledger as a SessionOutput before render (storage precedes rendering). The spike verifies the write occurs; it does not invent a parallel session store.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-033">SSE streaming rides the ChatInvocationContext streaming side channel — the spike observes this path, it does not create a bespoke stream.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">PaneEventBus payloads are typed discriminants (compose_action_request), no `any`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Throwaway only — no production code committed; the Action + Binding rows are throwaway and MUST NOT be deployed to a shared catalog beyond what the spike needs to observe the path. Deliverable is a spike note.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ai/session-dispatch, ai/session-ledger, ai/streaming</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-033-streaming-chat-tool-side-channel.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + load">Load this task, project CLAUDE.md, and the knowledge files. State the Placement Justification if any BFF surface is touched (expected: none new — path already exists).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Author throwaway Binding">Mirror-first: create a throwaway compose-explain-clause Action row (SystemPrompt + minimal OutputSchemaJson) + one Binding row targeting it under infra/dataverse/inputschemas/. Keep it minimal — the payload is not the point; the path is.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Wire stub toolbar">Add a stub Workspace toolbar button that emits a PaneEventBus compose_action_request event carrying {bindingId, selection, args}. Record the exact event shape.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Trace the chain">Confirm ConversationPane consumes the event, assembles the scope payload + selection args, and calls dispatchConsumer(bindingId, args) → POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{id}/dispatch.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Observe SSE + ledger">Confirm the response streams via SSE into the chat surface AND a SessionOutput ledger entry is written. Confirm the gate does not interfere for a Tier-0/1 action.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Write spike note">Record the decision + the Compose-specific contracts (event shape, args assembly, scope payload) in the spike note. Note any surprises that change Phase 1/3/4 assumptions.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
