  <notes>
    Completed 2026-07-08 (static code trace + contract reconciliation). Deliverable:
    notes/spikes/spike-0-dispatch-path.md.

    DECISION: The shipped ADR-039 session-dispatch seam is confirmed present + coherent
    end-to-end for a Compose Binding (server route unconditional, orchestrator resolves the
    Binding table, ADR-040 ledger-before-render, shared SSE writer, one client helper). ZERO
    new BFF dispatch routes needed.

    KEY CORRECTION (changes Phase 1/3/4): the design/POML `compose_action_request`
    `{bindingId, selection, args}` event DOES NOT EXIST and must not be created. The real,
    R1-shipped contract is the six-flow choreography in Spaarke.Compose.Components
    compose-contracts.ts — a selection emits `conversation.compose_selection_offer` (Flow 2);
    the actual dispatch is a direct `dispatchConsumer(bindingId, {slots})` call (the shipped
    useConsumerChips pattern); Assistant→editor insertion is `workspace.compose_assistant_insert`
    (Flow 5). Tasks 016/030/046 must be authored against this, not `compose_action_request`.

    Also confirmed: the parallel Compose AI-dispatch endpoint (POST /api/compose/action/
    {consumerType}) is DELETED (design §2.1/§7.2 premise holds); only a stale doc-comment
    survives at IComposeService.cs:35 (minor Phase-4/5 cleanup). R7 LinearConsumers and the
    session-dispatch seam are the same routing surface (sprk_playbookconsumer table), not rivals.

    CAVEAT: criteria 3 (SSE) + 4 (ledger write) are statically confirmed (wiring correct) but
    NOT live-observed — a headless code session cannot render live frames/rows. Runtime
    confirmation recipe recorded in the note §6 (run on spaarkedev1 at Phase 1 start; needs a
    throwaway Binding — core-A0-gated). Deliberately did not author/commit throwaway rows or
    stub UI (directional step-mode adaptation; rationale in note §7).
  </notes>
</task>
